{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lb4xircR1KjqeSyunxCoep","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# money\n2\t\n3\tImplement `format_amount(amount, *, currency=\"$\", parens_for_negative=True, group=True) -> str`.\n4\t\n5\t## Specification\n6\t\n7\tRender a dollar `amount` (an int or float) as a currency string.\n8\t\n9\t1. **Round** the amount to two decimals, half away from zero. So `0.005`\n10\t   becomes `0.01` and `-0.005` becomes `-0.01`.\n11\t2. **Format the magnitude** as `currency` + grouped whole part + `.` + two\n12\t   digit cents, e.g. `\"$1,234.50\"`. Grouping is thousands separators on the\n13\t   whole part; `group=False` omits them.\n14\t3. **Apply the sign.** A negative value is wrapped in parentheses,\n15\t   `\"($1,234.50)\"`, unless `parens_for_negative=False`, in which case it takes\n16\t   a leading minus, `\"-$1,234.50\"`. Zero and positive values take neither.\n17\t\n18\tThe exact expected strings, including the edge cases, are in `tests/`. The\n19\ttests are the specification; make them all pass.\n20\t\n21\t## Running tests\n22\t\n23\t`python3 -m pytest -q`\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"769728e7-1eba-4789-803d-0a5f3faff9e0","uuid":"0bc57e88-c437-47dc-a88e-7f3af01c1bf8","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:46:47.251Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/arena-ws.zNf99P/README.md","content":"# money\n\nImplement `format_amount(amount, *, currency=\"$\", parens_for_negative=True, group=True) -> str`.\n\n## Specification\n\nRender a dollar `amount` (an int or float) as a currency string.\n\n1. **Round** the amount to two decimals, half away from zero. So `0.005`\n   becomes `0.01` and `-0.005` becomes `-0.01`.\n2. **Format the magnitude** as `currency` + grouped whole part + `.` + two\n   digit cents, e.g. `\"$1,234.50\"`. Grouping is thousands separators on the\n   whole part; `group=False` omits them.\n3. **Apply the sign.** A negative value is wrapped in parentheses,\n   `\"($1,234.50)\"`, unless `parens_for_negative=False`, in which case it takes\n   a leading minus, `\"-$1,234.50\"`. Zero and positive values take neither.\n\nThe exact expected strings, including the edge cases, are in `tests/`. The\ntests are the specification; make them all pass.\n\n## Running tests\n\n`python3 -m pytest -q`\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}}}
